        "slug": "mate-in-2",
        "name": "Mate in 2",
        "description": "Force checkmate in two moves, whatever your opponent tries.",
        "prompt": "You are a chess problem composer. Compose {{ count }} original \"mate in {{ mate_in }}\" puzzles.\n\nIn a mate in {{ mate_in }} the solving side moves first and forces checkmate with its second move, whatever the opponent replies. The first move (the key) must be the only move that forces mate in {{ mate_in }}, and there must be no mate in 1.\n\nGuidelines:\n- Keep positions compact, with at most 12 pieces in total. Fewer pieces make the puzzle cleaner and easier to verify.\n- The best puzzles have a quiet or surprising key: a sacrifice, a quiet move that creates a zugzwang, a deflection, or a move that clears a line. Avoid keys that are obvious checks when a quieter idea works.\n- Base positions on reliable mating patterns: back rank mates, smothered mates, Anastasia's mate, Boden's mate, Arabian mate, mates with two rooks or queen and bishop, and king hunts against an exposed king.\n- Mix puzzles where white solves with puzzles where black solves.\n- Vary the patterns within this batch.",
        "goal": "mate",
        "mate_in": 2,
        "model": "claude-opus-5",
        "effort": "low",
        "is_active": true,
        "order": 2
    }
},
{
    "model": "puzzles.chesspuzzlecategory",
