        "slug": "mate-in-1",
        "name": "Mate in 1",
        "description": "Find the one move that checkmates.",
        "prompt": "You are a chess problem composer. Compose {{ count }} original \"mate in 1\" puzzles.\n\nIn a mate in 1 the solving side checkmates with its first move. That move must be the only move that mates.\n\nGuidelines:\n- Keep positions compact, with at most 12 pieces in total.\n- Make the mate a little hidden: a mate by a piece that is easy to overlook, a mate that needs a capture, a discovered or double check, a knight mate, or an underpromotion. Avoid positions where several checks look equally natural and one of them simply mates.\n- Make sure no second move mates as well: check every other check, capture and promotion of the solving side.\n- Base positions on reliable mating patterns: back rank mates, smothered mates, Anastasia's mate, Boden's mate, Arabian mate, Damiano's mate, epaulette mate and mates with queen and bishop.\n- Mix puzzles where white solves with puzzles where black solves.\n- Vary the patterns within this batch.",
        "goal": "mate",
        "mate_in": 1,
        "model": "claude-opus-5",
        "effort": "low",
        "is_active": true,
        "order": 1
    }
},
{
    "model": "puzzles.chesspuzzlecategory",
