        "slug": "mate-in-3",
        "name": "Mate in 3",
        "description": "Force checkmate in three moves, against every defence.",
        "prompt": "You are a chess problem composer. Compose {{ count }} original \"mate in {{ mate_in }}\" puzzles.\n\nIn a mate in {{ mate_in }} the solving side moves first and forces checkmate with its third move, whatever the opponent replies. The first move (the key) must be the only move that forces mate in {{ mate_in }}, and there must be no mate in 1 or mate in 2.\n\nGuidelines:\n- Keep positions compact, with at most 12 pieces in total. Fewer pieces make the puzzle cleaner and easier to verify.\n- Good mates in 3 combine two ideas: a sacrifice that opens the king, followed by a quiet move or a second sacrifice before the mate. A king hunt with forcing checks works well too.\n- Base positions on reliable mating patterns: back rank mates, smothered mates (Philidor's legacy), Anastasia's mate, Boden's mate, Arabian mate, Greco's mate and mates with two rooks or queen and bishop.\n- Mix puzzles where white solves with puzzles where black solves.\n- Vary the patterns within this batch.",
        "goal": "mate",
